hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"528","Muhammad ibn Qudamah ibn A'yan narrated to us, Jarir narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Abdullah ibn Uwaymir, who said: I was with Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, and I pointed with my hand toward the cloud. He said: Do not do it, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade pointing to it."
"529","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade pointing to the rain."
"530","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us. Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to me that some people heard thunder and uttered the takbir. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear thunder, glorify Allah and do not utter the takbir."
